# Complete game runtime and rendering behavior before final assets

Finish game systems after the playable vertical slice and before the final asset
pass. Asset consumers must target stable runtime contracts rather than forcing
runtime behavior to emerge from whatever was converted first.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Complete traffic, pedestrians, cameras, interaction, damage, recovery,
  effects, audio, cinematics, loading, saves, profiles, and progression systems.
- [ ] Implement source-backed material and shader behavior needed by gameplay
  and faithful presentation without inventing PBR values.
- [ ] Complete runtime state transitions, event ordering, timing, and lifecycle
  behavior required by missions and menus.
- [ ] Add behavior-focused parity tests before content-specific asset polish.

## Dependencies

Depends on the default player and vehicle vertical slice.
